{"title":"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems\">2000 AMC 12 #1</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems\">2000 AMC 10 #1</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Verifying_the_dumb_Statement)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Verifying the dumb Statement)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the year <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, the United States will host the International Mathematical Olympiad.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be distinct positive integers such that the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d60d326ca073c7b21065096e22646dbb9e7ddaf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I \\cdot M \\cdot O = 2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"129\" height=\"13\" />.  What is the largest possible value of the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/5558323f7948efd75545bb0e8c0e37a3b1c1da44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I + M + O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f1438fb943d4a888cdeebdc31768e8a30e63ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 23 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 55 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 99 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 111 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 671$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"411\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28febb0f1ee871c054ec75f5849e6d26d28f9234.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 23 \\cdot 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>The largest factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />.  The only way to write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> as a product of three integers including <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/0/370bfea35051538da3d0a931d283e3eafc0e3995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, which is not allowed since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is repeated.\n</p><p>The second largest factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba780b20e670c394844f58e8630ee172cdfcfa9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 \\cdot 29 = 667$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />.  The only way to write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> as a product of three integers including <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14dccd418e90ee38050238d4581e670a02f6baa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$667$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28cf3d93010e3a0f48ea43064e49b70ccaed873f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$667 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, which is allowed.  In this case, the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3eaf811febf450ed694ae284cab9e49134335497.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$667 + 3 + 1 = 671$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The third largest factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ecbe714b5d7bbeec61db22b299315648f280a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 29 = 87$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />.  So, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> was written as a product of three integers without <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14dccd418e90ee38050238d4581e670a02f6baa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$667$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, the largest of the integers would be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711f5fc6f8d53d2565cff62b15f932f02e0dbc58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$87$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> and the sum must therefore be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2b5b001d120ed78f226ed5d50b1b1c06b490cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$671$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the largest possible sum of the three factors is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb33366bcee2c693c086b7a46976bf1b3ff6030d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 671}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"73\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Verifying_the_dumb_Statement.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Verifying_the_dumb_Statement)\">Solution 2 (Verifying the dumb Statement)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Verifying the dumb Statement)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we need to recognize that a number is going to be largest only if, of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor\" title=\"Factor\">factors</a>, two of them are small. If we want to make sure that this is correct, we could test with a smaller number, like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. It becomes much more clear that this is true, and in this situation, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/5558323f7948efd75545bb0e8c0e37a3b1c1da44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I + M + O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Now, we use this process on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/89476a1ee4318030939b99d59e36768ace1d83b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$667 * 3 * 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> as our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors.\nHence, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52d09a10365f6bc9d95dc2398c1febe5972595c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$667 + 3 + 1 = \\boxed{\\text{(E) 671.}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"187\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~armang32324\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum is the highest if two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor\" title=\"Factor\">factors</a> are the lowest.\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67b90b1db0bc10afa5b24aeca5d4d11a204fa2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 667 = 2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"131\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d85ff978b0e4a8c60373f7fe3a8e3f1e268b1a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+3+667=671 \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{\\text{(E) 671}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"249\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812bb007fad7fe5299685796e828c6836c63b9ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 0 + 0 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can eliminate all of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> answer choices because they are way too small and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1b2caa6d42542e87cb2a2323aa870b94f4696f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) 671}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"68\" height=\"30\" /> as our final answer.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HK9hhf9Vw68\">https://youtu.be/HK9hhf9Vw68</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YrAs8vadKMk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YrAs8vadKMk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSzsStkkYeA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aSzsStkkYeA</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<